-- L4 trap fixture (xmod-identity #1351 spine): the assertion is ENTIRELY about `bmod`
-- (Greetable/Widget/greet), an ordinary interface-method call with a live impl -- it never
-- reaches `definerShadowArgHead`'s mangled-emit-path arm, because it is not a standalone
-- shadow occurrence at all. `amod` is imported (bare -- binds no names) only to put its
-- definer shadow in the graph, so `mangledFunDefsPresentRef` is True on the emit path.
-- Hand-derived expected value: `greet (Widget "World")` = "Hello, " ++ "World" ++ "!" =
-- "Hello, World!" -- unaffected by anything in `amod`.
import amod
import bmod.{Greetable, greet, Widget(..)}

main = println (greet (Widget "World"))
